Using `.find()` inside the `.map()` loop on the `manifest` array creates O(n²) complexity, violating performance rules for data parsed from a file. Construct a `Map` before the loop to enable O(1) lookups.

Kody rule violation: [Prefer Map for lookups inside loops](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ce10e93-d8b7-45db-b84c-d30c91c4a658?teamId=ebb24108-be7e-4fd9-9346-f1f2c7c0b7f1)

```typescript
const manifestMap = new Map(manifest.map((m) => [m.route, m]));
return RENDER_ROUTES.map(({ path, marker }) => {
    const entry = manifestMap.get(path);
    if (!entry) {
        throw new Error(
            `route ${path} not found in permissions.route-manifest.json — regenerate with UPDATE_ROUTE_MANIFEST=1`,
        );
    }
    return { path, marker, expected: entry.expected };
});
```



<details>

<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>

```

File tests/e2e/scenarios/rbac-ui-render.ts:

Line 71 to 80:

According to team rules, using array search methods like `.find()` inside a loop (`.map()` in this case) on another array can lead to O(n²) complexity. Since `manifest` is dynamically parsed from a file and not explicitly a small constant (< 10 items), this violates the rule. Construct a `Map` before the `.map()` loop to enable O(1) lookups.

Suggested Code:

    const manifestMap = new Map(manifest.map((m) => [m.route, m]));
    return RENDER_ROUTES.map(({ path, marker }) => {
        const entry = manifestMap.get(path);
        if (!entry) {
            throw new Error(
                `route ${path} not found in permissions.route-manifest.json — regenerate with UPDATE_ROUTE_MANIFEST=1`,
            );
        }
        return { path, marker, expected: entry.expected };
    });

```

</details>


