There is no accompanying data migration script, which means all existing documents in the `pullRequests` collection still have `user.id` stored as a string. 

When the application loads an existing pull request document, Mongoose will attempt to cast the stored string ID to a number. If the ID is not a numeric string (e.g., a UUID from a provider like Bitbucket, or any other non-numeric identifier that might exist), the cast will result in `NaN`.

